        "original_id": "839357aa-7847-5a33-b56c-38d9d59164ce",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Cotton Mather\n- Places: New England, United States\n- Organizations: Harvard College, University of Glasgow, Royal Society\n- Roles: Puritan minister, author, pamphleteer\n- Topics: History of New England\n\nFacts:\n- New England is the oldest clearly defined region of the United States, and it predates the history of the United States by more than 150 years.\n- Cotton Mather was born on February 12, 1663, and died on February 13, 1728.\n- Cotton Mather received an A.B. from Harvard College in 1678.\n- Cotton Mather received an A.M. from Harvard College in 1681.\n- Cotton Mather received an honorary doctorate from the University of Glasgow in 1710.\n- Cotton Mather was a socially and politically influential New England Puritan minister, prolific author, and pamphleteer.\n- Cotton Mather was a Fellow of the Royal Society.",
